---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
    title="Hermes Mail Privacy Policy"
    description="Privacy policy for the private Hermes Mail email assistant."
    canonicalPath="/hermes-mail/privacy/"
>
    <article class="policy-page policy-page--document">
        <div class="container policy-page__inner">
            <nav class="policy-page__nav" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
                <a href="/">bruni.to</a>
                <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
                <a href="/hermes-mail/">Hermes Mail</a>
                <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
                <span>Privacy</span>
            </nav>

            <header class="policy-hero policy-hero--document">
                <p class="eyebrow">Effective September 5, 2026</p>
                <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
                <p class="policy-hero__lead">
                    Hermes Mail is a private email automation tool operated by
                    Bruno Farfán Miquel. This policy explains the Google user
                    data it accesses and how that data is handled.
                </p>
            </header>

            <div class="policy-document">
                <section>
                    <p class="policy-document__number" aria-hidden="true">01</p>
                    <div>
                        <h2>Scope</h2>
                        <p>
                            Hermes Mail is intended only for its owner and a
                            small number of personally known, explicitly
                            authorized account holders. It is not offered for
                            public signup or as a commercial email service.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </section>

                <section>
                    <p class="policy-document__number" aria-hidden="true">02</p>
                    <div>
                        <h2>Google data accessed</h2>
                        <p>
                            After an account holder grants OAuth consent, Hermes
                            Mail may access Gmail message metadata, message
                            contents, attachments, labels, and the ability to
                            send messages or move messages to Trash. It requests
                            the Gmail permissions needed for those functions.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </section>

                <section>
                    <p class="policy-document__number" aria-hidden="true">03</p>
                    <div>
                        <h2>How data is used</h2>
                        <p>
                            Google user data is used only to complete an
                            owner-requested task: listing, searching or reading
                            email; downloading a requested attachment; preparing
                            or sending a message; changing labels; or moving a
                            message to Trash. Sending and mailbox mutations
                            require a separate owner approval.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </section>

                <section>
                    <p class="policy-document__number" aria-hidden="true">04</p>
                    <div>
                        <h2>AI processing and sharing</h2>
                        <p>
                            When the owner requests analysis, drafting,
                            summarization, or another agent task, the relevant
                            email content may be transmitted to and processed by
                            the OpenAI model service selected by the owner.
                            OAuth client secrets and refresh tokens are not sent
                            to the model. Data is not sold, rented, shared for
                            advertising, or used to build advertising profiles.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </section>

                <section>
                    <p class="policy-document__number" aria-hidden="true">05</p>
                    <div>
                        <h2>Storage and retention</h2>
                        <p>
                            OAuth credentials are stored on a private server
                            behind restricted operating-system permissions.
                            Downloaded attachments and owner-selected outputs
                            remain until the owner removes them under the
                            system's normal storage and backup practices.
                            Operational records are retained only as needed for
                            security, troubleshooting, and approval auditing.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </section>

                <section>
                    <p class="policy-document__number" aria-hidden="true">06</p>
                    <div>
                        <h2>Control and deletion</h2>
                        <p>
                            Account holders can revoke Hermes Mail at any time
                            from their Google Account's third-party connections
                            page. They may also request deletion of locally
                            retained OAuth credentials, downloaded files, and
                            related application data by contacting the address
                            below.
                        </p>
                        <p>
                            <a
                                href="https://myaccount.google.com/connections"
                                target="_blank"
                                rel="noopener noreferrer"
                            >Manage Google Account connections ↗</a>
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </section>

                <section>
                    <p class="policy-document__number" aria-hidden="true">07</p>
                    <div>
                        <h2>Google API policy</h2>
                        <p>
                            Hermes Mail's use and transfer of information
                            received from Google APIs adheres to the
                            <a
                                href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy"
                                target="_blank"
                                rel="noopener noreferrer"
                            >Google API Services User Data Policy ↗</a>, including
                            its Limited Use requirements.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </section>

                <section>
                    <p class="policy-document__number" aria-hidden="true">08</p>
                    <div>
                        <h2>Contact and updates</h2>
                        <p>
                            Material changes will be reflected on this page with
                            an updated effective date. Questions or deletion
                            requests can be sent to
                            <a href="mailto:info@bruni.to">info@bruni.to</a>.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </section>
            </div>
        </div>
    </article>
</Layout>
